{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778614557905,"sessionID":"ses_1e25b39caffe14skcRyo0X0AJ0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"functions.bash:51","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -i \"qc\\|single.child\\|excluded_from_qc\" /home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json","description":"Search issue context for QC mentions"},"output":"      \"body\": \"## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Data source\\n- VeNom release h (Feb 2026), TermSubset sheet, Diagnosis subset\\n- 5,271 active diagnosis terms after filtering\\n- VeNom uses British English spelling; matching applies British-to-American conversion\\n- VeNom uses prefix `VeNom` (consistent with VBO), xref source is `MONDO:VeNom`\\n\\n### Phase 1: Data extraction (complete)\\n- Extracted VeNom Diagnosis terms to `data/venom_diagnosis_terms.tsv`\\n- Parsed parenthetical content into abbreviations, species qualifiers, and synonyms\\n- Extracted VeNom hierarchy from Relationship sheet\\n\\n### Phase 2: Matching VeNom → Mondo (complete)\\n- Full results in `data/venom_matching_results.tsv`\\n- Matching approach: normalized names, British-to-American spelling, VeNom \\\"X - Y\\\" subtype reversal, parenthetical synonym swaps\\n\\n| Category | Count | Description |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| NHA exact match | 195 | VeNom term already exists in Mondo non-human animal branch |\\n| Human analog found | 991 | No NHA term, but matching human/general disease exists |\\n| No match | 4,085 | No name/synonym match in Mondo |\\n\\n- 174 unique Mondo NHA terms matched (some have multiple VeNom xrefs due to VeNom duplicates/variants)\\n- 16 false positives identified and reclassified, including:\\n  - Subtype concepts that over-matched to generic parents (e.g., \\\"Cachexia - cancer\\\" ≠ cancer)\\n  - Clinical severity grades that are distinct from the base concept (PLE CCECAI scores)\\n  - Concepts that matched via synonym but are different diseases (e.g., \\\"Cataract - Morgagnian\\\" ≠ CPAMD8-related cataract)\\n  - Concepts where the VeNom term is a synonym but not an exact match (e.g., \\\"Spiking mortality syndrome\\\" ≠ poult enteritis mortality syndrome; \\\"Osteochondrosis (Juvenile osteochondritis, dyschondroplasia)\\\" has additional scope)\\n\\n### Phase 3: Three separate ROBOT templates\\n\\n#### Template 1: NHA exact matches — add xrefs and synonyms (complete)\\n- File: `data/ROBOT_add_venom_xrefs_nha_matches.tsv`\\n- 195 rows adding VeNom xrefs to 174 existing Mondo NHA terms\\n- Also adds VeNom term name as exact synonym where it differs (37 rows)\\n- Also adds abbreviation synonyms (26 rows)\\n- Includes mondo_label and venom_label columns for manual review\\n- Status: **ready for review**\\n\\n#### Template 2: Human analog matches — new NHA terms via cross-species analog pattern\\n- 991 VeNom terms where a human/general disease exists in Mondo\\n- New terms follow `nonhuman_disease.yaml` pattern: \\\"{human disease}, non-human animal\\\"\\n- Definition: \\\"{human disease} that occurs in non-human animals\\\"\\n- Each gets: VeNom xref, cross-species analog relationship, VeNom name as synonym\\n- Status: **not started**\\n\\n#### Template 3: New terms with no match\\n- 4,076 VeNom terms with no Mondo match\\n- Classify under existing NHA parents where possible using VeNom hierarchy\\n- Build hierarchy among new terms (e.g., \\\"cystitis, non-human animal\\\" parent of \\\"bacterial cystitis, non-human animal\\\")\\n- Apply taxon restrictions for species-specific terms (6 with explicit species qualifiers like \\\"(canine)\\\")\\n- Add `excluded_from_qc_check` for single-child terms\\n- Status: **not started**\\n\\n### Phase 4: QC and normalization\\n- Run `robot convert` syntax validation\\n- Run `sh run.sh make NORM && mv NORM mondo-edit.obo`\\n\\n### Notes\\n- Animal type flags (equine, farm, small animal, avian, exotics) are tracked in matching results for future subset annotations\\n- VeNom has ~2,407 subtype terms (contain \\\" - \\\") — many are location-specific variants\\n- ~4 administrative codes (\\\"DIAGNOSIS NOT MADE\\\", etc.) should be excluded from all templates\",\n","metadata":{"output":"      \"body\": \"## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Data source\\n- VeNom release h (Feb 2026), TermSubset sheet, Diagnosis subset\\n- 5,271 active diagnosis terms after filtering\\n- VeNom uses British English spelling; matching applies British-to-American conversion\\n- VeNom uses prefix `VeNom` (consistent with VBO), xref source is `MONDO:VeNom`\\n\\n### Phase 1: Data extraction (complete)\\n- Extracted VeNom Diagnosis terms to `data/venom_diagnosis_terms.tsv`\\n- Parsed parenthetical content into abbreviations, species qualifiers, and synonyms\\n- Extracted VeNom hierarchy from Relationship sheet\\n\\n### Phase 2: Matching VeNom → Mondo (complete)\\n- Full results in `data/venom_matching_results.tsv`\\n- Matching approach: normalized names, British-to-American spelling, VeNom \\\"X - Y\\\" subtype reversal, parenthetical synonym swaps\\n\\n| Category | Count | Description |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| NHA exact match | 195 | VeNom term already exists in Mondo non-human animal branch |\\n| Human analog found | 991 | No NHA term, but matching human/general disease exists |\\n| No match | 4,085 | No name/synonym match in Mondo |\\n\\n- 174 unique Mondo NHA terms matched (some have multiple VeNom xrefs due to VeNom duplicates/variants)\\n- 16 false positives identified and reclassified, including:\\n  - Subtype concepts that over-matched to generic parents (e.g., \\\"Cachexia - cancer\\\" ≠ cancer)\\n  - Clinical severity grades that are distinct from the base concept (PLE CCECAI scores)\\n  - Concepts that matched via synonym but are different diseases (e.g., \\\"Cataract - Morgagnian\\\" ≠ CPAMD8-related cataract)\\n  - Concepts where the VeNom term is a synonym but not an exact match (e.g., \\\"Spiking mortality syndrome\\\" ≠ poult enteritis mortality syndrome; \\\"Osteochondrosis (Juvenile osteochondritis, dyschondroplasia)\\\" has additional scope)\\n\\n### Phase 3: Three separate ROBOT templates\\n\\n#### Template 1: NHA exact matches — add xrefs and synonyms (complete)\\n- File: `data/ROBOT_add_venom_xrefs_nha_matches.tsv`\\n- 195 rows adding VeNom xrefs to 174 existing Mondo NHA terms\\n- Also adds VeNom term name as exact synonym where it differs (37 rows)\\n- Also adds abbreviation synonyms (26 rows)\\n- Includes mondo_label and venom_label columns for manual review\\n- Status: **ready for review**\\n\\n#### Template 2: Human analog matches — new NHA terms via cross-species analog pattern\\n- 991 VeNom terms where a human/general disease exists in Mondo\\n- New terms follow `nonhuman_disease.yaml` pattern: \\\"{human disease}, non-human animal\\\"\\n- Definition: \\\"{human disease} that occurs in non-human animals\\\"\\n- Each gets: VeNom xref, cross-species analog relationship, VeNom name as synonym\\n- Status: **not started**\\n\\n#### Template 3: New terms with no match\\n- 4,076 VeNom terms with no Mondo match\\n- Classify under existing NHA parents where possible using VeNom hierarchy\\n- Build hierarchy among new terms (e.g., \\\"cystitis, non-human animal\\\" parent of \\\"bacterial cystitis, non-human animal\\\")\\n- Apply taxon restrictions for species-specific terms (6 with explicit species qualifiers like \\\"(canine)\\\")\\n- Add `excluded_from_qc_check` for single-child terms\\n- Status: **not started**\\n\\n### Phase 4: QC and normalization\\n- Run `robot convert` syntax validation\\n- Run `sh run.sh make NORM && mv NORM mondo-edit.obo`\\n\\n### Notes\\n- Animal type flags (equine, farm, small animal, avian, exotics) are tracked in matching results for future subset annotations\\n- VeNom has ~2,407 subtype terms (contain \\\" - \\\") — many are location-specific variants\\n- ~4 administrative codes (\\\"DIAGNOSIS NOT MADE\\\", etc.) should be excluded from all templates\",\n","exit":0,"description":"Search issue context for QC mentions","truncated":false},"title":"Search issue context for QC mentions","time":{"start":1778614557893,"end":1778614557896}},"id":"prt_e1db055a10015q02GBUipE5Btp","sessionID":"ses_1e25b39caffe14skcRyo0X0AJ0","messageID":"msg_e1dafbd2800124zOD31ynd3eeG"}}
